# Story 51: Running Bash (40s)
# Hook: Ask in plain English, and the agent runs the shell for you -- dangerous patterns ask first.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-051-running-bash.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Ask in plain English, and the agent runs the shell for you -- dangerous patterns ask first.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh and switch over to the agent.

[00:08.0 --> 00:13.0]
Double-press Escape for prompt mode.

[00:13.0 --> 00:30.0]
Ask what's using your disk. The agent calls the bash tool to run a real shell command and reads the output back to you. Safe, read-only commands just run -- but anything matching a dangerous pattern needs your approval first.

[00:30.0 --> 00:37.0]
That approval gate is what makes the bash tool safe: deletes, force-pushes, and other risky commands stop and wait for a yes before they ever execute.

[00:37.0 --> 00:40.0]
Natural language in, real shell commands out -- with a safety net.

